  "adaptations": [
    "Use the LLVM23 Toolhelp32 module map while preserving loader spelling; the newer GetLoadedModulePath helper is absent.",
    "Keep extended DOS/UNC prefix normalization local because LLVM23 predates Host/windows/PathUtils.h.",
    "Use explicit IPv4 loopback for TCPSocket::CreatePair on this host; no Windows network policy changes.",
    "Port the queued-events predecessor active-exception mutex, shared lifetime and predicate initialization from DebuggerThread.cpp at upstream commit814524c0dd2a93726e0d71a15532a0eba5eb1340. Already-continued events must clear the active exception so Resume releases the deferred-stop gate.",
    "Local fix: reconcile the event cache with EnumProcessModulesEx and a32768-character GetModuleFileNameExW buffer. Toolhelp32 paths truncate at MAX_PATH, and parallel loader speculation can otherwise hide the winning mapping. Preserve valid loader spelling for known physical bases. Source-evidence: source-c traces omit the actual runtime and long-e DAP launches exit42 without hitting an unresolved DLL breakpoint."
  ],
